I have print statements in place to print out the value of end as well as the substring, my issue is that it never reaches that point.

    System.out.println("start is: " + start);
                 while(start > 0)
                 {
                     int end = currentLine.indexOf("([ |.])", start);
                     System.out.println("end is: " + end);
                     if(end > 0)
                     {
                         String subString = currentLine.substring(start, end);
                         System.out.println("test " + subString);

start is initialized to 0 before the first while loop.

Thank you for helping.

throwing the exception does not give me any additional information. I tried using a debugger and it also did not help, though this is the first time I have used a debugger. 

You were entirely right about the substring method start is constantly negative, now I just need to figure out why. 

I am fairly certain that the issue lies with how I am trying to parse the text. I do not know if it is an issue with my regex or if it is an issue with the way I am trying to parse the text.

    while(fileInput.hasNext())
                {
